  "definition": "A User Interface (UI) is the set of visual, auditory, and interactive components through which a human operates a software system. In spatial and metaverse contexts, UIs extend beyond flat screens to encompass 3D menus, gesture controls, voice interfaces, and haptic feedback, mediated by head-mounted displays, handheld controllers, or bare-hand tracking. Effective UI design balances accessibility, cognitive load, and rendering performance, drawing on human-computer interaction principles and user experience research.",
